# Line-ending policy for this project's launchers.
#
# Without this file, each user's local `core.autocrlf` setting decides the
# line endings on checkout — which silently breaks platform-specific scripts:
#   * a .bat / .cmd with LF-only endings can make Windows cmd.exe misbehave
#     (stale-label jumps, broken multi-line blocks).
#   * a .command / .sh with CRLF endings fails on macOS/Linux with errors
#     like "\r: command not found" or "bad interpreter".
#
# Pinning eol here forces the correct endings on every machine regardless of
# the user's git config, so nobody has to touch core.autocrlf.

# Default: let git normalise text in the repo, native endings on checkout.
* text=auto

# Windows batch launchers -> always CRLF in the working tree.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Unix shell launchers -> always LF in the working tree.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf

# Treat known binaries as binary (no eol conversion, no diff noise).
*.pdf       binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.png       binary
